ed-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(2,1,-10)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(2,1)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(2,1) & =3(2) \\\\ & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(2,1)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(2,1)}(x-(2)) \\\\ z-(-10) & =(6)(x-(2)) \\\\ z & =6 x - 22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(2,1,-10)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=1 \\\\ z &=6 x - 22\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518860 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cefab39-ceab-5bc8-b0a6-6589512c35f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=- \\pi \\\\ z &=- \\left(1 - \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518841} {:answer/id #uuid "2436b4d1-ecfb-59f4-aa6f-855069b04715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=- \\pi \\\\ z &=- \\left(1 - \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right) - 11\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518845} {:answer/id #uuid "73e698a6-6d04-547c-9b5f-4ec276a6998c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=- \\pi \\\\ z &=\\left(1 - \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right) - 11\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518866} {:answer/id #uuid "db31537a-46f7-5cd1-b388-050def923915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3 \\\\ z &=- \\left(1 - \\pi\\right) \\left(y + \\pi\\right) - 