=- x + \\pi x - 3 \\pi - 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(3,- \\pi,-11)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=- \\pi \\\\ z &=- x + \\pi x - 3 \\pi - 8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bdd34ee-d34f-545e-b799-2be0655df4f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=2 \\pi \\\\ z &=- \\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right) + 12\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518856} {:answer/id #uuid "9b744279-4786-539e-8b14-a0ac7dcaa614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=2 \\pi \\\\ z &=\\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right) + 12\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518877} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ee9880-1460-507f-9f47-0b486e7219c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=2 \\pi \\\\ z &=\\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518884} {:answer/id #uuid "f5691efd-ed01-5d63-8ae5-b7036767a2f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3 \\\\ z &=\\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right) \\left(y - 2 \\pi\\right) + 12\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518901} {:answer/id #uuid "f72a30b8-ab34-560b-a74a-809ba598eb19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=2 \\pi \\\\ z &=\\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right) \\left(x + 3\\right) + 12\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b744279-4786-539e-8b14-a0ac7dcaa614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=2 \\pi \\\\ z &=\\left(1 + 2 \\pi\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right) + 12\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518877} :answer-field/id #uuid "29c535fc-40c1-5c8a-8618-286ea91174e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "767e873f-9d5e-53b8-a351-ac97e9472597" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=2 \\pi.$ Given that the point $P(3,2 \\pi,12)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=y \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=2 \\pi.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(3,2 \\pi,12)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(3,2 \\pi)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(3,2 \\pi):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(3,2 \\pi) & =(2 \\pi)\\cos((3)(2 \\pi))+\\cos(2 \\pi) \\\\ & =(2 \\pi)(1)+(1) \\\\ & =1 + 2 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(3,2 \\pi)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(3,2 \\pi)}(x-(3)) \\\\ z-(12) & =(1 + 2 \\pi)(x-(3)) \\\\ z & =x + 2 \\pi x - 6 \\pi + 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(3,2 \\pi,12)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=2 \\pi \\\\ z &=x + 2 \\pi x - 6 \\pi + 9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0105290b-487b-5f1f-9501-389134f1bca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begi