 the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(3,1,11)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(3,1)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(3,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(3,1) & =-4(3) \\\\ & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(3,1)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(3,1)}(x-(3)) \\\\ z-(11) & =(-12)(x-(3)) \\\\ z & =47 - 12 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(3,1,11)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=1 \\\\ z &=47 - 12 x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518874 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02deddff-9059-5e47-9c26-85eaba82b228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=2 \\\\ z &=24 - 8 x\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518835} {:answer/id #uuid "25dc159f-2b25-5616-b689-0949e232380b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2 \\\\ z &=24 - 8 y\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518846} {:answer/id #uuid "4595568e-9c5b-5c6a-b50a-4e0976745cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=2 \\\\ z &=- 8 x - 8\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518855} {:answer/id #uuid "6e88bdab-5911-5cd6-bc3d-20f02fa8a250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=2 \\\\ z &=8 x + 24\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518862} {:answer/id #uuid "fb77957b-ee3e-5ce8-a221-053fc85456f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{align