- 3 \\pi)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(2,- 3 \\pi):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(2,- 3 \\pi) & =(- 3 \\pi)\\cos((2)(- 3 \\pi))+\\cos(- 3 \\pi) \\\\ & =(- 3 \\pi)(1.0)+(-1.0) \\\\ & =- 3.0 \\pi - 1.0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(2,- 3 \\pi)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(2,- 3 \\pi)}(x-(2)) \\\\ z-(5) & =(- 3 \\pi - 1)(x-(2)) \\\\ z & =- 3 \\pi x - x + 7 + 6 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(2,- 3 \\pi,5)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=- 3 \\pi \\\\ z &=- 3 \\pi x - x + 7 + 6 \\pi\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65e5c3f0-5773-5bbd-a23a-3a43d1fc086e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531761} {:answer/id #uuid "6b202fc5-7a82-5091-9da5-936069a8528b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{727}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531763} {:answer/id #uuid "9e2a14ab-0cce-5725-9c80-5f9d2f8d0921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "182" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531782} {:answer/id #uuid "bf400e9b-bb0b-5054-8ef9-7e5f7d9ae05b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "197" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531789} {:answer/id #uuid "f958d464-4ab0-5f12-8833-fb278b8eb146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{713}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f958d464-4ab0-5f12-8833-fb278b8eb146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{713}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531799} :answ