an be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{x=3 \\\\ z=3 - 2 y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=3,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=3 - 2 y$ (or $- 2 y - z + 3=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,-2,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,-2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =j - 2 k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $⟨0,1,-2⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556132 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37dd67a6-9302-52ce-a4eb-b458c3c38495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,-8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556115} {:answer/id #uuid "7c4acddb-f393-5ef8-8512-f2734c2b7b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,8,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556136} {:answer/id #uuid "87120362-d259-56d3-979a-9bd2346dda46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,8,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556139} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c1d413-8151-5d44-94fe-2a943194fc87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556151} {:answer/id #uuid "c164c3ce-a97a-5789-ae86-81689ef5e741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c164c3ce-a97a-5789-ae86-81689ef5e741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556153} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4340bac-2429-5c45-a387-f044a1812b92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "76fc75e5-bc34-5a11-827a-718027bfa6d6" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=1.$ Given that the point $P(1,2,-3)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=8$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(1,2).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,2) & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(1,2) & ={f}_{y}(1,2)(y-(2)) \\\\ z-(-3) & =(8)(y-(2)) \\\\ z-(-3) & =8 y - 16 \\\\ z & =8 y - 19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,2,-3)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{x=1 \\\\ z=8 y - 19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=1,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=8 y - 19$ (or $8 y - z - 19=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,8,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,8,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =j + 8 k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $⟨0,1,8⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556140 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49af77ba-23b1-5c02-ae78-e0a7f3dcabf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,2,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556119} {:answer/id #uuid "5a03e80c-0292-50fe-a3ba-354f93996f82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556125} {:answer/id #uuid "63614bc9-8e20-5bf1-8110-d978ebea603a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556128} {:answer/id #uuid "dfefda43-a9c6-542a-aa55-6d293ada18bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556161} {:answer/id #uuid "ee0f23c0-bab4-5a6d-b985-d5db0527d0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfefda43-a9c6-542a-aa55-6d293ada18bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556161} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9ff40d2-36af-55fb-8db5-205b757e863c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "87773f30-7347-58c3-bc15-641532470ff8" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=-3.$ Given that the point $P(-3,3,-1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=2$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=-3.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(-3,3).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(-3,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-3,3) & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(-3,3) & ={f}_{y}(-3,3)(y-(3)) \\\\ z-(-1) & =(2)(y-(3)) \\\\ z-(-1) & =2 y - 6 \\\\ z & =2 y - 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-3,3,-1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{x=-3 \\\\ z=2 y - 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=-3,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=2 y - 7$ (or $2 y - z - 7=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,2,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =j + 2 k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $⟨0,1,2⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556144 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a2d6f59-2293-503c-954b-099ede3ec4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,16,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556106} {:answer/id #uuid "550d8d58-5825-568a-904a-a283edc87093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,16⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556122} {:answer/id #uuid "91cf613e-e775-536e-b2b2-d6c5690147d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,-16⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556145} {:answer/id #uuid "c5f9d2d0-aacd-5bf3-bbfb-0fba361f5592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556154} {:answer/id #uuid "d6acb0ee-9654-5419-9420-f6821a5f49f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,16,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556158}] :answ