- 1 + \\pi\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707672 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3516b060-4b13-5212-a2a5-74c5f5270515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=2 y + 1\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707662} {:answer/id #uuid "92f2cba2-94d2-5ab3-8a70-ad6f25dbfce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=2 y + 3\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707675} {:answer/id #uuid "a292c2d3-14a6-5f30-8282-8aef52ca3370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=7 - 2 y\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707677} {:answer/id #uuid "aaae8776-0ccf-56d7-b1c6-15956ed3120a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707678} {:answer/id #uuid "bda0317f-fcb7-587f-be42-193c6e9b0e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaae8776-0ccf-56d7-b1c6-15956ed3120a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707678} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee610454-3cd2-5a0f-a31a-8d7438b40c81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6a4f7fe6-ac55-54e4-b160-ecfafd2211f5" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=2$. The point $P(2,1,3)$ lies on $C$, and\n\n$$\nf_y(x,y)=-\\left(x{e}^{x\\left(y - 1\\right)}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(y - 1\\right)\\right)\n$$\n\nFind the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P$." :question/worked-solution "The plane fixes $x$, so $y$ varies along the section. Evaluate the supplied partial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m&=f_y(2,1) \\\\ &=-\\left(\\left(2\\right){e}^{\\left(2\\right)\\left(\\left(1\\right) - 1\\right)}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\left(1\\right) - 1\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse point-slope form at $(y_0,z_0)=(1,3)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-(3)&=(0)(y-(1)) \\\\ z&=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe tangent retains the fixed-coordinate plane:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707682 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15298f7e-edcd-5deb-97bd-a28ad9ead78a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=1 \\\\ z &=6 x - 2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707654} {:answer/id #uuid "28bcefb5-649b-53fc-b527-b2012af3c51b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=1 \\\\ z &=3 x - 5\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707658} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce3b34d-972a-5b11-8afe-62038eed65b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=1 \\\\ z &=3 x - 2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707669} {:answer/id #uuid "6955a72b-83ad-542c-9c41-6eafc5b10184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=1 \\\\ z &=6 x - 5\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707671} {:answer/id #uuid "e9989c34-f791-5270-97c9-6fe3fb39df4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=1 \\\\ z &=- 3 x - 2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ce3b34d-972a-5b11-8afe-62038eed65b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=1 \\\\ z &=3 x - 2\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707669} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d870e04-9d46-5116-82c1-94f372657e6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c3a4751f-3bd5-57ec-9574-6c3c4347a5c3" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=1$. The point $P(1,1,1)$ lies on $C$, and\n\n$$\nf_x(x,y)=3x+6x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\n$$\n\nFind the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P$." :question/worked-solution "The plane fixes $y$, so $x$ varies along the section. Evaluate the supplied partial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m&=f_x(1,1) \\\\ &=3\\left(1\\right)+6\\left(1\\right)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\left(1\\right)\\left(1\\right)) \\\\ &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse point-slope form at $(x_0,z_0)=(1,1)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-(1)&=(3)(x-(1)) \\\\ z&=3 x - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe tangent retains the fixed-coordinate plane:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=1 \\\\ z &=3 x - 2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707684 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cd85cab-9fd7-56f6-8711-7afdd6c581cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=-2 \\\\ z &=4 x + 7\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707659} {:answer/id #uuid "59560962-4f0a-570e-b934-c2dc5edfddaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=-2 \\\\ z &=7 - 2 x\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707668} {:answer/id #uuid "8225f140-8f26-556a-a18f-219c81a3e5d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=-2 \\\\ z &=- 2 x - 11\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707674} {:answer/id #uuid "b965bda9-8685-5f0b-a000-25ad05060d36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=-2 \\\\ z &=4 x - 11\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707680} {:answer/id #uuid "e562604c-e8e4-57bf-956a-00232d2b5435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=-2 \\\\ z &=- 4 x - 11\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59560962-4f0a-570e-b934-c2dc5edfddaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=-2 \\\\ z &=7 - 2 x\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707668} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbea1afe-45d6-5409-a344-5b862d9ad06a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e43c0ca6-d98a-50c2-a136-e5b1dd1d407f" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=-2$. The point $P(3,-2,1)$ lies on $C$, and\n\n$$\nf_x(x,y)=-\\left({y}^{2}\\left(x - 1\\right)+2y-\\left(x - 1\\right)\\right)\n$$\n\nFind the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P$." :question/worked-solution "The plane fixes $y$, so $x$ varies along the section. Evaluate the supplied partial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m&=f_x(3,-2) \\\\ &=-\\left({\\left(-2\\right)}^{2}\\left(\\left(3\\right) - 1\\right)+2\\left(-2\\right)-\\left(\\left(3\\right) - 1\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse point-slope form at $(x_0,z_0)=(3,1)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-(1)&=(-2)(x-(3)) \\\\ z&=7 - 2 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe tangent retains the fixed-coordinate plane:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=-2 \\\\ z &=7 - 2 x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17e7c8fb-8a83-5ac4-8abb-13d97f116b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 3,0,\\frac{18}{13}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707765} {:answer/id #uuid "3d30d925-d58a-528f-9959-d24a423a2aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -2,0,\\frac{6}{13}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707771} {:answer/id #uuid "67075c53-7e42-56b5-8fdc-4b9877040650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -3,0,- \\frac{9}{13}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707781} {:answer/id #uuid "b19d4e69-bbe9-5beb-a844-710b86a74171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -1,0,0\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707787} {:answer/id #uuid "ff34cb4a-4d73-5d88-8d1b-42dfc8a3c78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -1,0,4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67075c53-7e42-56b5-8fdc-4b9877040650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -3,0,- \\frac{9}{13}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707781} :answer-field/id #uuid "339702a9-dd54-5e7b-9497-6975c31fcbac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "074fb8c2-fd96-5d84-90e7-baf7c5d8a421" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=5$. The point $P(-4,5,3)$ lies on $C$. The partial derivative is supplied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_x(x,y) & =-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}}{2x-y}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$?" :question/worked-solution "Holding $y$ fixed means that $x$ varies, so the slice slope is $f_x(-4,5)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=f_x(-4,5) & =-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{{\\left(5\\right)}^{2}-{\\left(-4\\right)}^{2}}}{2\\left(-4\\right)-\\left(5\\right)}\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{3}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe displayed quotient is evaluated at the supplied point; its denominator is nonzero. Simplifying the numerator and denominator gives the exact slope above.\n\nA change of $1$ in $x$ along the tangent gives a change of $\\frac{3}{13}$ in $z$, with no change in $y$. A tangent direction is $\\langle 1,0,\\frac{3}{13}\\rangle$.\n\nThe tangent line through $P(-4,5,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y&=5 \\\\ z-(3)&=\\left(\\frac{3}{13}\\right)(x-(-4))\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe second plane is equivalently $\\frac{3 x}{13} - z + \\frac{51}{13}=0$. Normal vectors are $\\mathbf n_1=\\langle 0,1,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf n_2=\\langle - \\frac{3}{13},0,1\\rangle$. Their cross product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf n_1\\times\\mathbf n_2 & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ - \\frac{3}{13} & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ & =\\langle 1,0,\\frac{3}{13}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAny nonzero scalar multiple is valid. The listed answer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\left(\\langle 1,0,\\frac{3}{13}\\rangle\\right) & =\\langle -3,0,- \\frac{9}{13}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt has the required component ratio $v_z/v_x=\\frac{3}{13}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707768 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e9afe5f-70f1-5c86-9824-0bb46ae97aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -3,0,9\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707766} {:answer/id #uuid "72d7e9e6-68c2-5963-8013-322172f953fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -1,0,\\frac{1}{3}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707784} {:answer/id #uuid "7dda25df-97ac-532f-9a9a-22cb8e8532b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 2,0,0\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707785} {:answer/id #uuid "a93b7079-5521-534f-8450-86f5bdc995a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -2,0,4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707786} {:answer/id #uuid "bd4723ab-3930-555a-a78d-9c773f2639d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -3,0,\\frac{9}{2}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e9afe5f-70f1-5c86-9824-0bb46ae97aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle -3,0,9\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707766} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ea4dbfe-e77d-574e-8cc8-9bf29dbcc3bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "323509f0-f65f-5236-9b49-00b7d77c64b0" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=-1$. The point $P(1,-1,-3)$ lies on $C$. The partial derivative is supplied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_x(x,y) & =-\\left(3{e}^{x+y}-\\ln |xy|\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$?" :question/worked-solution "Holding $y$ fixed means that $x$ varies, so the slice slope is $f_x(1,-1)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=f_x(1,-1) & =-\\left(3{e}^{\\left(1\\right)+\\left(-1\\right)}-\\ln |\\left(1\\right)\\left(-1\\right)|\\right) \\\\ & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA change of $1$ in $x$ along the tangent gives a change of $-3$ in $z$, with no change in $y$. A tangent direction is $\\langle 1,0,-3\\rangle$.\n\nThe tangent line through $P(1,-1,-3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y&=-1 \\\\ z-(-3)&=(-3)(x-(1))\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe second plane is equivalently $- 3 x - z=0$. Normal vectors are $\\mathbf n_1=\\langle 0,1,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf n_2=\\langle 3,0,1\\rangle$. Their cross product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf n_1\\times\\mathbf n_2 & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ & =\\langle 1,0,-3\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAny nonzero scalar multiple is valid. The listed answer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\left(\\langle 1,0,-3\\rangle\\right) & =\\langle -3,0,9\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt has the required component ratio $v_z/v_x=-3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707770 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065e779b-0a32-5f45-9aa1-8405b9541573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-3,-6\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707762} {:answer/id #uuid "4d7a4bd6-fa4e-53d4-aa6c-e20eed50430a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-2,-1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707773} {:answer/id #uuid "4e7e4fdc-ca8b-5c2b-8cb8-30a880dfb5fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-2,0\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707774} {:answer/id #uuid "507a7732-ae52-5ae6-925b-ebce245518b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-1,-4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707775} {:answer/id #uuid "5c08add4-2688-5939-a5fb-7ddc8917fef8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-1,2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "065e779b-0a32-5f45-9aa1-8405b9541573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-3,-6\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707762} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8edbd6d-9795-553f-a879-683aba32909e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "37ad2f20-2071-5b02-9bda-5a1b03b52c58" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=0$. The point $P(0,0,-2)$ lies on $C$. The partial derivative is supplied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_y(x,y) & =-\\left(2(y+x)-2\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$?" :question/worked-solution "Holding $x$ fixed means that $y$ varies, so the slice slope is $f_y(0,0)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=f_y(0,0) & =-\\left(2(\\left(0\\right)+\\left(0\\right))-2\\right) \\\\ & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA change of $1$ in $y$ along the tangent gives a change of $2$ in $z$, with no change in $x$. A tangent direction is $\\langle 0,1,2\\rangle$.\n\nThe tangent line through $P(0,0,-2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x&=0 \\\\ z-(-2)&=(2)(y-(0))\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe second plane is equivalently $2 y - z - 2=0$. Normal vectors are $\\mathbf n_1=\\langle 1,0,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf n_2=\\langle 0,-2,1\\rangle$. Their cross product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf n_1\\times\\mathbf n_2 & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ & =\\langle 0,-1,-2\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNegating this cross product gives $\\langle 0,1,2\\rangle$.\n\nAny nonzero scalar multiple is valid. The listed answer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\left(\\langle 0,1,2\\rangle\\right) & =\\langle 0,-3,-6\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt has the required component ratio $v_z/v_y=2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707790 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "140a0c9c-5ddf-5e97-9cf2-08623d2f49dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,2,-4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707764} {:answer/id #uuid "307e35f4-f814-5485-92bc-037dc17d6b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-2,- 3 \\sqrt{2}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707767} {:answer/id #uuid "5bfa23c1-10d5-575f-adca-735373bba2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-1,- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707777} {:answer/id #uuid "d6925a9c-c6c6-5fc0-bd0e-1d2a87ec6ad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,3,- \\frac{15 \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707791} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f260a4-c909-52d8-94e8-0df98a901873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-2,-2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "307e35f4-f814-5485-92bc-037dc17d6b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-2,- 3 \\sqrt{2}\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707767} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0aa99c9-526a-58f9-82de-9c41e9ec77ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cba914e7-7c8a-5902-80e2-2c2c483b8c05" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=-2$. The point $P(-2,1,-2)$ lies on $C$. The partial derivative is supplied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_y(x,y) & =\\frac{y-x}{\\sqrt{x(y+x)}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$?" :question/worked-solution "Holding $x$ fixed means that $y$ varies, so the slice slope is $f_y(-2,1)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=f_y(-2,1) & =\\frac{\\left(1\\right)-\\left(-2\\right)}{\\sqrt{\\left(-2\\right)(\\left(1\\right)+\\left(-2\\right))}} \\\\ & =\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe displayed quotient is evaluated at the supplied point; its denominator is nonzero. Simplifying the numerator and denominator gives the exact slope above.\n\nA change of $1$ in $y$ along the tangent gives a change of $\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}$ in $z$, with no change in $x$. A tangent direction is $\\langle 0,1,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\rangle$.\n\nThe tangent line through $P(-2,1,-2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x&=-2 \\\\ z-(-2)&=\\left(\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)(y-(1))\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe second plane is equivalently $\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2} y}{2} - z - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} - 2=0$. Normal vectors are $\\mathbf n_1=\\langle 1,0,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf n_2=\\langle 0,- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2},1\\rangle$. Their cross product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf n_1\\times\\mathbf n_2 & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ & =\\langle 0,-1,- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNegating this cross product gives $\\langle 0,1,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\rangle$.\n\nAny nonzero scalar multiple is valid. The listed answer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2\\left(\\langle 0,1,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\rangle\\right) & =\\langle 0,-2,- 3 \\sqrt{2}\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt has the required component ratio $v_z/v_y=\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707793 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44333c84-37ff-5088-a2bb-c0c1fe749c37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,3,9\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707772} {:answer/id #uuid "5e592ea2-f503-5a7c-b647-dd990cccd8be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-1,-5\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707779} {:answer/id #uuid "67c440a0-e34f-5440-b111-ac46e5c8109e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,2,2\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707782} {:answer/id #uuid "67d51087-7948-5261-bf8b-986061c9baf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-3,9\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707783} {:answer/id #uuid "fe9a6071-29be-5599-a82c-6d29641a0ad3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,3,30\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e592ea2-f503-5a7c-b647-dd990cccd8be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,-1,-5\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707779} :answer-field/id #uuid "55832f69-3d2d-53b6-8118-ade9cbf63a04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "eedad1b7-9544-57ae-9fb3-f2540fe036bc" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=2$. The point $P(2,-1,2)$ lies on $C$. The partial derivative is supplied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_y(x,y) & ={y}^{2}+{x}^{2}-\\ln (y+x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$?" :question/worked-solution "Holding $x$ fixed means that $y$ varies, so the slice slope is $f_y(2,-1)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=f_y(2,-1) & ={\\left(-1\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(2\\right)}^{2}-\\ln (\\left(-1\\right)+\\left(2\\right)) \\\\ & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA change of $1$ in $y$ along the tangent gives a change of $5$ in $z$, with no change in $x$. A tangent direction is $\\langle 0,1,5\\rangle$.\n\nThe tangent line through $P(2,-1,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x&=2 \\\\ z-(2)&=(5)(y-(-1))\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe second plane is equivalently $5 y - z + 7=0$. Normal vectors are $\\mathbf n_1=\\langle 1,0,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf n_2=\\langle 0,-5,1\\rangle$. Their cross product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf n_1\\times\\mathbf n_2 & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ & =\\langle 0,-1,-5\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNegating this cross product gives $\\langle 0,1,5\\rangle$.\n\nAny nonzero scalar multiple is valid. The listed answer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1\\left(\\langle 0,1,5\\rangle\\right) & =\\langle 0,-1,-5\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt has the required component ratio $v_z/v_y=5$."}]}
